  "identifier": "gow-ragnarok-complete-guide-2026",
  "headline": "God of War Ragnarok Complete Guide Blueprint: A repeatable plan for builds, exploration, and boss pages",
  "description": "A guide design that scales: difficulty-based progression rules, combat fundamentals that always work, and a fixed boss-article template so you can produce consistent, high-quality walkthrough content.",
  "articleBody": "This is a blueprint for writing and executing a full God of War Ragnarok strategy guide. The point is not to list every item, but to define repeatable rules: (1) what to prioritize, (2) what combat patterns stay stable across fights, and (3) a consistent boss-page format that keeps guides readable and actionable.\n\n1. Pick your goal\n- Story-first: minimize detours, solve only hard blockers\n- Exploration-first: collect upgrades early to widen build options\n- High-difficulty-first: minimize hits taken, optimize gauge loops (weapon buffs, rage, cooldowns)\n\n2. Progression rules by difficulty\n- Low to mid: lean into damage and cooldown, keep at least one reliable healing option\n- High: remove one-shot risk with defense/resist/consistency, prefer short and safe runics\n- Universal: when stuck, upgrade weapon/shield/runics first; level gaps spike difficulty more than most perks\n\n3. Combat fundamentals (the real win conditions)\n- Read order: unblockables first, then AoE and projectile speed\n- Two dodges: short-step for spacing, roll for hard resets; do not over-roll\n- Lock a defensive style: mostly parry, mostly evade, or mostly guard; mixing too much slows decisions\n- Keep the loop: maintain weapon buff uptime, spend runics from the most reliable to land first\n- Do not get greedy: one safe punish then reset beats long strings on high difficulty\n\n4. Build design by role (not by item names)\n- Stable: mitigation + sustain + cooldown; forgives mistakes\n- Burst: cooldown loop + conditional bonus damage; wins short windows\n- Break/control: stun/interrupt focus; ideal for crowds\n- Status control: element/poison/freeze style to reduce enemy actions\n\n5. Exploration design\n- Prefer guaranteed power (upgrade materials) over completion for its own sake\n- Suggested priority: weapon upgrades > runics/relics > armor refresh > full collection\n- If lost: secure shortcuts and the merchant first; create a clean upgrade path\n\n6. Boss article template (use this for every fight)\n- Summary: recommended level band, common failure mode\n- Prep: shield type, relic role, runics chosen for safety\n- Threat recognition: unblockable, tracking, delay, AoE\n- Punish windows: list only 3 consistent openings\n- Spacing plan: preferred range and why\n- Phase notes: what changes at health thresholds\n- Recovery plan: how to reset, where healing is safe\n- High-difficulty alternative: a more stable variant (short runics, safer relic)\n\n7. Headings that scale into a full guide set\n- Beginner: decision priority and basic reads\n- Intermediate: gauge loops, runic rotation, companion usage\n- Advanced: zero-hit patterns, punish-only wins, consistency builds\n\nIf you follow this blueprint, you can grow Ragnarok coverage into a coherent set: a central guide, build pages, exploration checklists, and boss pages that all share the same vocabulary and structure.",
